A||N||16||Cplensdorf||Car Covers.  Anybody using them?||||1||
Z||000000||Cplensdorf||07-08-2001||11:22 AM||||Well... I am getting back my GT after a months worth of prep and paint and rubbing.  I am looking for a quality car cover for it to protect the paint when I get it back.  Anybody have any comments on a manufacturer, etc. for this?  It needs to be an outdoor type.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Old Lar||07-08-2001||11:41 AM||||I've been using a cover I get from Pepboys.  It is a breathable fabric.  Pricy devil at $129.  They last a couple of years.  Some fine dust gets washed through during the rain.  In the winter I cover the car, car cover with a waterproof tarp.  Seems to work for me.||||reg||1
Z||000002||turbo86se||07-08-2001||12:00 PM||||I just use a Budge dust cover for my 86SE in the garage. I think it cost me $30 at Advance.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Robert||07-08-2001||01:16 PM||||<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/P3310010_1.JPG"> <P>------------------<BR>           <IMG SRC="http://canterburytrails.com/photo/T2.GIF">  <P> "By the time you die, you should be so used to <BR>paying taxes that it would be almost second nature <BR>to you."<P>Will Rogers, U.S. Writer and Humorist||||reg||1
