Z||000006||rogergarrison||07-08-2001||07:10 PM||||USE EXTREME CAUTION !!!!!! new paint takes several months to fully cure. If you put a cover on fresh paint the sun will cook it into the paint. Moisture wont help either. Youll get off ez if you just have fabric imprint on the finish. Lots ive seen simply pull off the paint thats stuck to the inside of cover. WHEN YOU DO USE IT SAFELY, good idea to take it off once in a while to let it air out, even if you dont drive it.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Cplensdorf||07-08-2001||09:14 PM||||Roger,<P>Just found that out today while reading the warranty for a cover, thanks.  I think the idea of baking a $200 cover to my car after a $2500 paint job doesn't sound so good.  What else will I have to be careful for after the new paint?  I may go with a portable car port/canopy.  I can get one for around $200.  I just do not want bird crap on my car before I can wax it.  When will I be able to wax it?  ||||reg||1
Z||000008||Robert||07-08-2001||10:12 PM||||My wife bought me the cover, and I never did see the bill, so I don’t know how much it cost.  It did come from an advertiser in the back on an auto magazine.  Here is a link to the site that handles them.  <BR> <A HREF="http://www.saddleman.com/wolf/wolfcovers/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.saddleman.com/wolf/wolfcovers/</A> <BR> <BR>Wolf is the brand, Noah is the material.  It is custom fitted to my car, so it always looks tight.  I’ve had it for a couple of years now and it still works fine. It is pretty thick, so it takes up a lot of room in the trunk.  I waited six months after the new paint job before using it, it has never left a mark on the car.||||reg||1
Z||000009||rogergarrison||07-09-2001||07:37 AM||||I recommend not using any wax for at least 30 days. Remove bird droppings as soon as possible, the acid in it burns right into the paint.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Fierochic88||07-09-2001||08:45 AM||||I have the Fiero Store car cover with the Fiero GT Emblem on the front.  It fits well and seems to protect the car pretty well.  Though they can sometimes be a pain to deal with I was happy with the service I got on the cover.<P>Jennifer<P>------------------<BR>IM Username:  FieroChic88<BR>Silver 1988 GT<BR>Silver 1986 2m4<BR>Cobalt Blue 85 GT<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.webjolt.f2s.com/pictures/jenscar-sig1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000011||Tom88gt||07-09-2001||09:12 AM||||Harbor Freight Tools sells a nice heavy duty canopy/carport for $129.99 (no tax and free shipping) on sale right now (usually $199) #40544-2CHA.  This is the same one that Wal-Mart and K-mart sell for about $180-200 + tax.||||reg||4
